```
=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router6
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the static default route on router6 (FRR staticd / zebra
routing table). The router runs RIP and correctly learns all explicitly announced
subnets (172.16.x, 192.168.x, 10.x, etc.) via its single RIP peer router3
(10.50.1.1 on eth2/link r6_r3). However, the FRR running configuration contains
no static route whatsoever, and router3's RIP process has no
"default-information originate" directive — meaning no default route is being
injected into RIP either. As a result, router6's kernel FIB contains only the
12 specific RIP-learned prefixes and its 3 directly connected subnets; the
0.0.0.0/0 entry is completely absent. Any packet destined for a prefix not
explicitly listed (any truly external or unknown destination) hits no matching
FIB entry and is silently dropped in the kernel. Intra-Location-B traffic and
RIP-learned destinations continue to work because those specific prefixes are
present; only the "catch-all" path is missing.

Root cause: the static default route `ip route 0.0.0.0/0 10.50.1.1` was
removed from router6 during the recent config change.

Corrective fix: restore the static default route on router6 by running the
following in vtysh:
  configure terminal
  ip route 0.0.0.0/0 10.50.1.1
  exit
  write memory
This re-installs 10.50.1.1 (router3) as the gateway of last resort, restoring
reachability to all destinations not covered by RIP-learned routes.
=== END ===
```